# Heart events and friend-day scenes for the slice villagers (docs/narrative/EVENTS.md). Compiled to zz_fs_slice_events.json.

dialogue wren.openmic
n0 wren: Well? Be honest. A performer needs one honest face in the crowd. Today you're the whole crowd.
  ? Cheer like forty people. => r0 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.wren.openmic.cheer
  ? Heckle, but kindly. => r1 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.wren.openmic.heckle
  ? Hide behind the menu. => r2 | flag:choice.wren.openmic.hide
r0 wren: Oh, I could live on that. Do it again. Louder. Pretend the porch is full.
  expr happy
r1 wren: A heckler! At last, I'm a real act. You're going in the second verse.
  expr happy
r2 wren: Fair. I'd hide too. Come out, though. The second verse is worse, and you'll want to see it.


dialogue wren.kitchen
n0 wren: It needs one more thing. Pepper, a splash of cider, or do we leave it alone and back away slowly?
  ? Pepper. Be brave. => r0 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.wren.kitchen.pepper
  ? A splash of cider. => r1 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.wren.kitchen.cider
  ? Plain. It's already good. => r2 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.wren.kitchen.plain
r0 wren: Brave it is! If I cry, blame the pepper. Officially, it was always the pepper.
  emote sweat
r1 wren: Cider. Sweet, with a little mischief in it. Like most of my regulars.
r2 wren: Plain? You think it's already good? Nobody has ever said that about my cooking. I'm keeping you.
  expr happy


dialogue wren.bag
n0 wren: There's a bag under my bar. Packed since the day I arrived. I haven't opened it in years, and I haven't unpacked it either.
  expr thinking
  next n1
n1 wren: I came here to rest for one season. That was eight years ago. So tell me. Go, stay, or leave it under there?
  ? Go. See what's out there. => r0 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.wren.bag.go
  ? Stay. We'd all miss you. => r1 | friend:wren,10 | flag:choice.wren.bag.stay
  ? Say nothing. Just listen. => r2 | friend:wren,15 | flag:choice.wren.bag.listen
r0 wren: Go. Just like that. You say it like it's easy. ...Maybe it is. I'd want a very good map.
r1 wren: Stay. Oh. That's a nicer word than I expected. I'll keep it in the bag, next to the socks.
r2 wren: ...You didn't tell me what to do. Everyone has advice for the one behind the bar. You just let me talk.
  expr sad


dialogue hazel.swap
n0 hazel: What would you lend me? (I'm not choosing for you. I'm leaning slightly.)
  ? The book I love best. => r0 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.hazel.swap.book
  ? A recipe card, if that counts. => r1 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.hazel.swap.recipe
  ? Honestly? I don't read much. => r2 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.hazel.swap.honest
r0 hazel: Oh. (It's a both-hands book.) I'll read it twice. Once for the story, once for you.
  expr happy
r1 hazel: A recipe. (A book without a spine.) I'll shelve it under Fiction until I bake it.
r2 hazel: Thank you for saying so. (Most people pretend.) I'll find something short. There's a heron in it.


dialogue hazel.hiding
n0 hazel: The festival wants someone to read aloud. Ione said my name. (I've been back here since ten.) Is that strange?
  expr thinking
  ? Ask what she hears back here. => r0 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.hazel.hiding.ask
  ? Sit down beside her, quietly. => r1 | friend:hazel,15 | flag:choice.hazel.hiding.wait
  ? Joke that she could hide in a book. => r2 | friend:hazel,5 | flag:choice.hazel.hiding.joke
r0 hazel: Pages turning, two rooms away. Other people's thoughts, kept. (It never asks me to read aloud.)
r1 hazel: ...Oh. (Nobody's ever sat down. They usually say 'there you are'.)
  expr happy
r2 hazel: Ha. (A small one.) I tried that once. The book was too thin.


dialogue hazel.rehearsal
n0 hazel: ...and so the lamp burned lower, and nobody minded. (That's the end.) What did you hear?
  expr embarrassed
  ? It was lovely. => r0 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.hazel.rehearsal.praise
  ? The middle dragged a little. => r1 | friend:hazel,15 | flag:choice.hazel.rehearsal.critique
  ? Laugh gently at the lamp. => r2 | friend:hazel,10 | flag:choice.hazel.rehearsal.laugh
r0 hazel: Lovely. (I'm going to press that word in a book.) Thank you.
  expr happy
r1 hazel: The middle. (I knew it. Lines five through eight.) Thank you for saying it out loud.
r2 hazel: The lamp is a bit much. (It's meant to be.) It stays. It's my only regular listener.


dialogue bram.repair
n0 bram: Old hoe. Split socket, blade's still good. Hold it, strike it, or watch?
  ? Hold it steady for him. => r0 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bram.repair.hold
  ? Ask to swing the hammer. => r1 | friend:bram,15 | flag:choice.bram.repair.hammer
  ? Watch from a safe distance. => r2 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bram.repair.watch
r0 bram: Don't grip. Hold. ...Hm. Like that.
r1 bram: Square on. Again. ...Hm. The iron believed you.
  expr happy
r2 bram: Hm. Watch the edge, not me. Juno watches me. Bad habit.


dialogue bram.long
n0 bram: I worked alone for years, told myself I liked it, and lied. Then you kept sitting down. I wrote my teacher thirty letters. Sent none.
  expr thinking
  ? Say nothing. Nod. => r0 | friend:bram,15 | flag:choice.bram.long.nod
  ? Tell him you're glad he said it. => r1 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bram.long.glad
  ? Answer with one word. => r2 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bram.long.word
r0 bram: ...Hm. A nod. That's how my teacher said yes.
r1 bram: Glad. Hm. Good word. I'll keep it.
  expr happy
r2 bram: One word. ...Hm. That's all I ever wanted back.


dialogue bram.juno
n0 bram: A horseshoe. Crooked by a thumb. She's out back, pretending not to wait. What do I say?
  ? Tell her it's wonderful. => r0 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bram.juno.praise
  ? Tease her about the crook. => r1 | friend:bram,10 | flag:choice.bram.juno.tease
  ? Ask what he sees in it. => r2 | friend:bram,15 | flag:choice.bram.juno.ask
r0 bram: Wonderful. Hm. Crooked and wonderful. Both true. I can say both.
r1 bram: Hm. Tease. I can do that. Teasing's just praise with a dent.
  expr happy
r2 bram: ...Hm. Me. My first shoe was crooked the same way.
  expr sad

